        "create_time": 1776862016.893943,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Ah—now I see what you mean: **entity[\"software\",\"Google Apps Script\",\"JavaScript platform for Google Workspace\"] (GAS)**, not GSAP.\n\nHere’s the straight answer:\n\n👉 **You cannot convert a 2D website into a true 3D mesh-based website using Google Apps Script.**\n\n---\n\n## ❌ Why GAS won’t do real 3D\nGoogle Apps Script is designed for:\n- Automating entity[\"software\",\"Google Sheets\",\"spreadsheet app\"]  \n- Building simple web apps (HTML Service)  \n- Handling forms, emails, data  \n\nBut it **does NOT support**:\n- WebGL rendering  \n- Mesh creation  \n- Real-time 3D engines  \n\nSo no:\n- ❌ Three.js rendering inside GAS backend  \n- ❌ GPU-based 3D scenes  \n- ❌ Game-like environments  \n\n---\n\n## ✅ What you *can* do with GAS\nYou *can* still build a system that **connects your website to Google Sheets**, like:\n\n### 1. Use GAS as backend (data layer)\n- Store users, inventory, listings in Sheets  \n- Use GAS as API  \n\nExample:\n```javascript\nfunction doGet() {\n  return ContentService.createTextOutput(\"Hello from GAS backend\");\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Build frontend separately (this is key)\nYour 3D site should live outside GAS using:\n- entity[\"software\",\"Three.js\",\"JavaScript 3D library\"]  \n- entity[\"software\",\"GSAP\",\"GreenSock Animation Platform\"]  \n\nThen connect it to GAS via HTTP requests.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Combine them (this is the real solution)\n\n**Architecture:**\n```\n[3D Website (Three.js + GSAP)]\n            ↓\n     fetch() API calls\n            ↓\n[Google Apps Script Web App]\n            ↓\n     Google Sheets (database)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Simple integration example\n\n### GAS (backend)\n```javascript\nfunction doGet() {\n  const data = {\n    property: \"Condo A\",\n    price: 500000\n  };\n  return ContentService\n    .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify(data))\n    .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Frontend (3D site)\n```javascript\nfetch(\"YOUR_GAS_WEB_APP_URL\")\n  .then(res => res.json())\n  .then(data => {\n    console.log(data);\n\n    // Use data in 3D scene\n    cube.position.x = data.price / 100000;\n  });\n```\n\n---\n\n## 💡 Best approach for YOU\nSince you want:\n- login  \n- inventory  \n- property system  \n\n👉 Use GAS for:\n- Database (Sheets)  \n- Emails  \n- Automation  \n\n👉 Use real frontend for:\n- UI  \n- 3D visualization  \n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Reality check\nTrying to build a full 3D app **inside GAS HTML Service** will:\n- Break performance  \n- Be extremely limited  \n- Not scale  \n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Bottom line\n- GAS = backend / automation  \n- 3D = external frontend (Three.js)  \n- You connect them via APIs  \n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can:\n- Build you a **Google Sheets-powered backend**\n- AND a **3D condo viewer frontend connected to it**\n\nStep-by-step, using only what you’re comfortable with 👍"
          ]
        },
